# Demo configuration for docker compose.
#
#   cp demo.env .env      (Windows: copy demo.env .env)
#
# Compose auto-loads .env for *every* command, so these settings survive the
# dependency resolution that a `docker compose run sim` triggers -- which a
# shell-exported variable does not. See DEMO_GUIDE.md.

# Honour X-Forwarded-For so the simulator's clients present distinct sources.
# Off in normal operation (a spoofable source header defeats behavioural
# detection); on here because the whole point of the harness is many clients.
TRUST_PROXY=1

# Attach the detection scores to every response header, so the simulator can
# record what benign traffic scored, not only what was blocked.
DETECTION_TRACE=1

# The stack's behaviour is already the shipping default (hybrid, threshold 0.7,
# noisy-OR). Uncomment to demonstrate a baseline configuration instead:
# DETECTION_MODE=rules
# DETECTION_MODE=off

# Only needed on a laptop that PULLS the images instead of building them from
# source (see DEMO_GUIDE.md "Shipping this project to another laptop"). Must
# match the Docker Hub account the images were pushed to, or `docker compose
# up` falls back to a placeholder name that does not exist and the pull fails.
# DOCKERHUB_USER=your-dockerhub-username
